# The review of step 23, the golden screens: the dialogs of screens 2a to
# 2d are the application's own frames, so a change to the answers it
# offers, their order, their labels, the dialog's chrome or its fitting to
# the window changes a reference screen. Before, the screens drew the
# dialogs from the views with the test's own answer list and every row of
# detail, and none of these was compared.

[break] the-note-answer-first
rule: An approval's answers are in the order the core offers its choices, "deny with a note" last (screen 2a).
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/dialog.rs
in: Dialog::answers
find: answers.push(act(Action::DenyWithNote, "Deny with a note"));
replace: answers.insert(0, act(Action::DenyWithNote, "Deny with a note"));
caught-by:
    cortex-tui::it screens::the_views_draw_the_reference_screens

[break] trust-answers-reordered
rule: The trust question's answers are "Trust it", "Not now", "Never for this project", in that order (screen 2c).
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/dialog.rs
in: Dialog::answers
find:
    answers.push(act(Action::Deny, "Not now"));
    answers.push(act(Action::Never, "Never for this project"));
replace:
    answers.push(act(Action::Never, "Never for this project"));
    answers.push(act(Action::Deny, "Not now"));
caught-by:
    cortex-tui::it screens::the_views_draw_the_reference_screens

[break] a-label-reworded
rule: The answer that allows for the session says "Allow this session", as the reference screen does.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/dialog.rs
in: Dialog::answers
find: (Action::AllowSession, "Allow this session")
replace: (Action::AllowSession, "Allow for this session")
caught-by:
    cortex-tui::it screens::the_views_draw_the_reference_screens

[break] no-blank-row-above-the-hint
rule: A dialog has a blank row between its answers and the hint row when the window has six rows or more.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::frame
find:
    if chrome {
        bottom.push(Line::new());
replace:
    if chrome {
caught-by:
    cortex-tui::it screens::the_views_draw_the_reference_screens

[break] the-chrome-takes-a-row-more
rule: A dialog may take every row of the window but the blank row and the hint row: one that fits that exactly is drawn whole (screen 2c).
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::frame
find: self.rows - 2
replace: self.rows - 3
caught-by:
    cortex-tui::it screens::the_views_draw_the_reference_screens

[break] a-dialog-that-fits-exactly-is-cut
rule: A dialog's detail gives way only when the dialog is taller than its room, not when it fills it exactly (screen 2c).
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/dialog.rs
in: Dialog::draw
find: let over = fitted.lines.len().saturating_sub(rows);
replace: let over = fitted.lines.len().saturating_sub(rows.saturating_sub(1));
caught-by:
    cortex-tui::it screens::the_views_draw_the_reference_screens
